<title>UK: TABLE - BAA yr pretax profit off after charge.</title>
<headline>TABLE - BAA yr pretax profit off after charge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		28.4		   vs 30.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 7.9		    vs 7.125</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 12.4		   vs 11.25</p>
<p> Pretax		     407		    vs 418</p>
<p> Exceptional gains	3.0		    vs 15</p>
<p> Exceptional charges    40.0		   vs nil</p>
<p> Turnover		   1,373		  vs 1,253</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 440-460 million stg before exceptionals.</p>
<p>The airports operator announced in April it would cease to capitalise interest on preparatory expenditure for its 1.5 billion stg project to build a fifth passenger terminal at London Heathrow because of delays in winning planning permission, although the expenditure itself would continue to be capitalised.</p>
<p>As a result, it was taking an exceptional interest charge of 40 million stg to write off the interest already capitalised and increased interest payable by 13 million stg for the year just ended.</p>
<p>Full company name - BAA Plc</p>
</text>
